      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CORMORAN STRIKE NZ (6) is racing well this prep having won three of his last four starts, including last time out over 1609m at this track when leading all of the way as the odds-on favourite. Won't find this much harder and can go back-to-back. PESCO POLLO (7) made it two straight wins last start when scoring as the favourite over 1609m at this track after racing outside the leader for most of the trip after having started from the same draw as today. Looks the main danger to the top selection. GANDHI MAIL (8) is an ex Italian trained colt who led all of the way here to score over 2300m two runs back in what was his first start in Australian start. Only finished sixth here last start but had no luck in the running after racing wide early and then racing outside the leader as the $2.25 favourite. Worth another chance. I AM HELLBOUND (10) finished second in a Group 3 event over 2680m at Albion Park last start when leading for most of the trip. Easier here and looks hard to roll.",
